Composite-scroll-sync v3: lock-only.

Build 421 still stalled (rendering-update cycle went quiescent after the
first scroll: updateRendering / requestComposition / displayDidRefresh all
stopped firing). Two lessons from 420/421:
 - Walking the scrolling tree (applyLayerPositions) from the COMPOSITOR
   thread pokes thread-owned machinery and stalls the rendering-update
   cycle; don't do it.
 - LayerTreeHost::notifyCompositionRequired IS legitimately called on the
   compositor thread upstream (CoordinatedPlatformLayer::updateBackingStore
   "tiles changed"); the 421 suppression ate that signal. Restore upstream
   behaviour.

What remains — and what actually fixes the sticky-navbar jitter — is
holding ScrollingTree::treeLock() across the compositor's layer-state
flush: the scrolling thread's scroll-then-compensate walk (scroll
boundsOrigin first, then fixed/sticky position compensation, both under
the tree lock) becomes atomic with respect to composites, so no frame can
render a fresh scroll offset against a stale sticky position. Stale
main-thread sticky commits are already corrected upstream by
Page::finalizeRenderingUpdate(ApplyScrollingTreeLayerPositions) before the
composite is requested, inside the same lock discipline.

Applies on top of webkit-sticky-scroll-composite-sync-env.patch +
webkit-composite-scroll-sync-stall-fix.patch.
ScrollingTree::applyLayerPositionsWhileLocked() becomes unused but is kept.

diff -u -r a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/LayerTreeHost.cpp /tmp/claude-0/-root/f7982d7a-a9a3-4363-bf41-0bd830f80d10/scratchpad/patchwork/d/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/LayerTreeHost.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/LayerTreeHost.cpp	2026-07-02 12:03:06.709203783 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/LayerTreeHost.cpp	2026-07-02 12:26:40.871227752 +0000
@@ -411,15 +411,6 @@
         m_compositionRequiredInScrollingThread = true;
         return;
     }
-    // Layer position changes applied by the compositor thread itself right
-    // before its layer flush (WEBKIT_COMPOSITE_SCROLL_SYNC) are consumed by
